# API overview

This page introduces the HTTP API foundation generated for `{{ service_name }}` and points to the
canonical contract pages for authoring service operations.

## Transport and operations

FastAPI owns HTTP routing, request validation, response serialization, and OpenAPI generation. The
root path is the sole non-RPC path. Public service methods otherwise use RPC-style operation IDs and
matching paths; their exact naming and body rules are defined in the
[RPC contract](rpc-contract.md).

An RPC accepts one named, typed JSON request body when it needs input. A parameterless operation
omits the body. Transport details do not become application or domain values: a route translates a
validated request into application input and translates the application result into a public
response model.

## Responses and errors

Every operation returns the four-field [`ApplicationResponse`](application-response.md) envelope.
The envelope distinguishes success from failure while keeping the successful result strongly
typed. Central exception handlers convert the supported failure categories into safe public
responses described in [API errors](errors.md).

## OpenAPI and generated clients

The service disables FastAPI's built-in schema and documentation URLs. It publishes the generated
OpenAPI 3.1 document inside `ApplicationResponse` through `GET /openapi.get`. The document is the
input to the authoritative `pypokerlost` method generator; PokerLost inter-service calls use the
generated methods and SDK client rather than a service-owned HTTP transport. See
[OpenAPI and SDK](openapi-and-sdk.md) for the publication and client boundary.

The pristine endpoint inventory is maintained in the
[public surface manifest](public-surface.md). A concrete service updates that manifest and the
relevant canonical contract page whenever its API changes.
